.netlify/

# Nothing here today, but a secret is only committed once. The relay
# function reads its keys from Netlify environment variables, and these
# patterns keep a local copy of them from following.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
serviceAccount.json

.DS_Store

# Saved copies of other people's sites, kept locally as layout reference.
# These must never be committed: anything in this repo is published, so a
# competitor's page would end up served from navrenagency.com.
www_*.html
*_reference.html

# Raw drops of a final asset before it's cropped/converted/renamed into the
# kebab-case JPEG pair the site actually uses. Every real asset in images/
# is kebab-case with no spaces (README convention - a space becomes %20 and
# breaks the URL), so "has a space in the name" is a clean, general test for
# "this is a drop waiting to be converted," not a site asset. Kept on disk
# as the source, never committed: these also run tens of MB uncompressed,
# which the "full JPEG, sm JPEG" pattern everywhere else in images/ exists
# specifically to avoid shipping.
images/* *.png
images/* *.jpg
images/* *.jpeg
